     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p16-information",
     "replacement": "The **compounding frequency** is the number of times per year that interest is calculated and added to the balance. The compounding frequency, number of periods and rate per period must match.\n\nNumber of periods:\t**Multiply** the number of years by the compounding frequency.\nRate per period:\t**Divide** the annual interest rate by the compounding frequency.\n\nMonthly means 12 times a year\n\nQuarterly means 4 times a year\n\nSemi-annually, half-yearly or bi-annually means 2 times a year (every 6 months)",
